{"id": "EUVD-2026-103471", "enisaUuid": "496dc2dd-bdbd-3c6e-90c1-9297504dcf70", "description": "cgltf through 1.15 contains a heap out-of-bounds write vulnerability in cgltf_accessor_unpack_floats() that allows attackers to write outside the output buffer via unchecked sparse accessor indices. Attackers can supply a crafted glTF or GLB file with large sparse indices to corrupt heap memory, crash applications, and potentially execute code when cgltf_validate() is not called.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:36:59", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/cgltf-accessor-unpack-floats-sparse-oob", "https://github.com/jkuhlmann/cgltf/blob/360db1a95480fe102ae9c69b27c5d101167ff5ba/cgltf.h#L2436-L2441", "https://github.com/jkuhlmann/cgltf", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/cgltf-through-1.15-heap-out-of-bounds-write-via-cgltf-accessor-unpack-floats"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6vjv-6x7m-3wjx", "CVE-2026-112018"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a5d1f2ff-7688-380c-be9c-105fd14df4ab", "product": {"name": "cgltf", "vendor": {"name": "jkuhlmann"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4b19fc62-c21b-39fb-8636-4e591e614c1f", "vendor": {"name": "jkuhlmann"}}], "isExploited": false}